{"case": "own-wl-036", "search_mode": "unavailable", "sources": ["web_tool.py curl 2026-11-06T13:47:27.392699+00:00"], "complete": true, "pages": [{"url": "https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_autoindex_module.html", "finalUrl": "https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_autoindex_module.html", "at": "2026-11-06T13:47:27.392699+00:00", "status": 200, "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "bytes": 7344, "body": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd\">\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Module ngx_http_autoindex_module</title><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../css/style_en.css\"></head><body><div id=\"banner\"><div id=\"banner-content\">\n\nNGINX will be at KubeCon North America, November 9–12 in Salt Lake City.\nVisit us at Booth 100! Check out our\n<a href=\"https://go.f5.net/kubecon-na-blog\">blog post</a>\nfor more details.\n\n</div></div><div id=\"main\"><div id=\"menu\"><input class=\"side-menu\" type=\"checkbox\" id=\"side-menu\"><label class=\"hamb\" for=\"side-menu\"><span class=\"hamb-line\"></span></label><nav class=\"nav\"><h1><a href=\"/\"><img src=\"/img/nginx_logo.svg\" alt=\"NGINX\" class=\"lightimage\" style=\"display: block; height: auto;\"><div class=\"darkimageWrapper\" style=\"mso-hide: all; display: none\"><img src=\"/img/nginx_logo_dark.svg\" alt=\"NGINX\" class=\"darkimage\" style=\"display: none;\"></div></a></h1><div><ul class=\"mobilemenu\"><li>english<br></li><li><a href=\"../../../ru/docs/http/ngx_http_autoindex_module.html\">русский</a></li><li><br></li><li><a href=\"../../../news.html\">news</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/\">about</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/download.html\">download</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/security_advisories.html\">security</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/docs/\">documentation</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/docs/faq.html\">faq</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/books.html\">books</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/community.html\">community</a></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/enterprise.html\">enterprise</a></li><li><br></li><li><a href=\"https://community.nginx.org\">community forum (new)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://x.com/nginxorg\">x.com</a></li><li><a href=\"https://blog.nginx.org/\">blog</a></li><li><br></li><li><a href=\"../../../en/docs/njs/\">njs</a></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/nginx/kubernetes-ingress\">ingress controller</a></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/nginx/nginx-gateway-fabric\">gateway fabric</a></li></ul></div></nav></div><div id=\"content\"><h2>Module ngx_http_autoindex_module</h2><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"><a href=\"#example\">Example Configuration</a><br><a href=\"#directives\">Directives</a><br>     <a href=\"#autoindex\">autoindex</a><br>     <a href=\"#autoindex_exact_size\">autoindex_exact_size</a><br>     <a href=\"#autoindex_format\">autoindex_format</a><br>     <a href=\"#autoindex_localtime\">autoindex_localtime</a><br></td></tr></table>\n\n<a name=\"summary\"></a><p>\nThe <code>ngx_http_autoindex_module</code> module processes requests\nending with the slash character (‘<code>/</code>’) and produces\na directory listing.\nUsually a request is passed to the <code>ngx_http_autoindex_module</code>\nmodule when the\n<a href=\"ngx_http_index_module.html\">ngx_http_index_module</a> module\ncannot find an index file.\n</p>\n\n\n<a name=\"example\"></a><center><h4>Example Configuration</h4></center><p>\n</p> <blockquote class=\"example\"><pre>\nlocation / {\n    autoindex on;\n}\n</pre></blockquote><p> \n</p>\n\n\n<a name=\"directives\"></a><center><h4>Directives</h4></center><a name=\"autoindex\"></a><div class=\"directive\"><table cellspacing=\"0\">\n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Syntax:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code><strong>autoindex</strong> <code>on</code> | <code>off</code>;</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Default:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <pre>autoindex off;</pre>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Context:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code>http</code>, <code>server</code>, <code>location</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            </table></div><p>\nEnables or disables the directory listing output.\n</p><a name=\"autoindex_exact_size\"></a><div class=\"directive\"><table cellspacing=\"0\">\n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Syntax:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code><strong>autoindex_exact_size</strong> <code>on</code> | <code>off</code>;</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Default:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <pre>autoindex_exact_size on;</pre>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Context:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code>http</code>, <code>server</code>, <code>location</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            </table></div><p>\nFor the HTML <a href=\"#autoindex_format\">format</a>,\nspecifies whether exact file sizes should be output in the directory listing,\nor rather rounded to kilobytes, megabytes, and gigabytes.\n</p><a name=\"autoindex_format\"></a><div class=\"directive\"><table cellspacing=\"0\">\n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Syntax:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code><strong>autoindex_format</strong> \n    <code>html</code> |\n    <code>xml</code> |\n    <code>json</code> |\n    <code>jsonp</code>;</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Default:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <pre>autoindex_format html;</pre>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Context:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code>http</code>, <code>server</code>, <code>location</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            </table><p>This directive appeared in version 1.7.9.\n            </p></div><p>\nSets the format of a directory listing.\n</p><p>\nWhen the JSONP format is used, the name of a callback function is set\nwith the <code>callback</code> request argument.\nIf the argument is missing or has an empty value,\nthen the JSON format is used.\n</p><p>\nThe XML output can be transformed using the\n<a href=\"ngx_http_xslt_module.html\">ngx_http_xslt_module</a> module.\n</p><a name=\"autoindex_localtime\"></a><div class=\"directive\"><table cellspacing=\"0\">\n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Syntax:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code><strong>autoindex_localtime</strong> <code>on</code> | <code>off</code>;</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Default:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <pre>autoindex_localtime off;</pre>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                <th>\n            Context:\n                </th>\n                <td>\n            <code>http</code>, <code>server</code>, <code>location</code><br>\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n            </table></div><p>\nFor the HTML <a href=\"#autoindex_format\">format</a>,\nspecifies whether times in the directory listing should be\noutput in the local time zone or UTC.\n</p>\n\n</div><div id=\"footer\">© F5, Inc. All rights reserved.</div></div></body></html>\n", "captured_by": "web_tool.py curl"}], "search": []}